# Merge drivers for append-mostly ledgers (#5436).
#
# `merge=union` keeps BOTH sides' lines on a conflicting hunk instead of stopping.
# It applies to LOCAL merges and rebases only: GitHub's mergeability check and
# merge button ignore .gitattributes, so a PR can still read CONFLICTING on
# GitHub while `git rebase origin/main` resolves it cleanly here. The structural
# fix for the hot ledgers is one file per entry (scripts/eval/experiments/) with
# EXPERIMENTS.md generated on main; union is the belt for the files that stay
# append-mostly.
#
# A row both sides EDITED is kept twice, adjacent — re-read the hunk after a rebase.
scripts/eval/DECISIONS.md               merge=union
scripts/eval/experiments/_series-*.md   merge=union
# Invariant docs that sessions append incidents to; flagged by
# scripts/audit/append-only-ledgers.mjs on 2026-10-01 (88% and 82% insertion-only).
.claude/docs/invariants/measurement-instruments.md  merge=union
.claude/docs/invariants/language-fields.md          merge=union
